Fix GCC 16 C++ build: mixed array designators in lightrec_map[].

The lightrec_map[] initializer designates the first six entries by index
([PSX_MAP_KERNEL_USER_RAM] = {...} etc.) but leaves the three mirror
entries positional. GCC 16 rejects mixing designated and non-designated
array initializer clauses in C++ ('either all initializer clauses should
be designated or none of them should be'). Give the mirror entries their
explicit PSX_MAP_MIRROR{1,2,3} designators; layout is unchanged.

diff --git a/mednafen/psx/cpu.cpp b/mednafen/psx/cpu.cpp
--- a/mednafen/psx/cpu.cpp
+++ b/mednafen/psx/cpu.cpp
@@ -3689,21 +3689,21 @@
 	},
 
 	/* Mirrors of the kernel/user memory */
-	{
+	[PSX_MAP_MIRROR1] = {
 		.pc = 0x00200000,
 		.length = 0x200000,
 		.address = NULL,
 		.ops = NULL,
 		.mirror_of = &lightrec_map[PSX_MAP_KERNEL_USER_RAM],
 	},
-	{
+	[PSX_MAP_MIRROR2] = {
 		.pc = 0x00400000,
 		.length = 0x200000,
 		.address = NULL,
 		.ops = NULL,
 		.mirror_of = &lightrec_map[PSX_MAP_KERNEL_USER_RAM],
 	},
-	{
+	[PSX_MAP_MIRROR3] = {
 		.pc = 0x00600000,
 		.length = 0x200000,
 		.address = NULL,
